    "body": "<p>This Signature model designs a coastal soundscape as a tidal system. Virtual waves are specified by period, virtual seabirds by call schedules, virtual underwater life by snap and chorus rates, and virtual boats by an anthrophony level, and the model computes wave rate per hour, waves per tidal half-cycle, and the underwater balance with and without boats. Tides are specified as a six-hour half-cycle that moves the virtual shoreline and changes wave loudness. The coast is invented, the boats are virtual, and any rendered coastal sound is labelled SIMULATED. Its purpose is teaching tidal soundscape rhythm and boat-noise masking in one design.</p><h4>Science proof</h4><p>Science proof: the model encodes the documented coastal pattern: wave periods set by swell and shore, seabird colonies, underwater fish and shrimp sound, tidal modulation of levels, and boat-noise masking. Those patterns are published coastal soundscape findings, reproduced here as a parameter-explicit design.</p><h4>Math proof</h4><p>Math proof: if virtual waves break every 10 seconds, the wave rate is 60 / 10 = 6.0 waves per minute, or 360 waves per hour, and 360 x 6 = 2160 waves in a 6-hour tidal half-cycle. The demo prints 6.0 waves per minute, 360 waves per hour, and 2160 waves per tidal half-cycle.</p><h4>Soundscape layer(s)</h4><p>biophony; geophony; anthrophony</p><h4>Source</h4><p>Signature design study for this database, October 2026; coastal soundscape pattern as in the public edition</p>",
